/**
 * Rajasthan silhouette background, a decorative, fully themeable illustration.
 *
 * This file is generated from a 83-shade warm illustration. None of the artwork's
 * colors are hardcoded on the paths: every fill references `RajasthanPalette`, so the
 * whole scene can be recolored to match the active theme.
 *
 * Two ways to theme it:
 *   1. `tone`   , pass a single base color; the entire ramp is rotated to that hue while
 *                  keeping each shade's original lightness (and relative saturation), so the
 *                  depth/shading of the artwork is preserved. This is the theme knob.
 *   2. `palette`, override any individual shade(s). Keys run `shade01` (lightest) →
 *                  `shade83` (darkest). Merged over whatever `tone` produced.
 *
 * Pure/presentational: no hooks, so it renders on the server (fine as a login background).
 *
 * @example
 *   <RajasthanBg className="w-full h-auto" />                    // original colors
 *   <RajasthanBg tone="hsl(var(--primary))" className="..." />   // theme-driven, see note below
 *   <RajasthanBg tone="#2563eb" />                               // recolor to any hex
 *   <RajasthanBg palette={{ shade01: "#fff" }} />                // tweak one shade
 *
 * NOTE: `tone` needs a resolvable color (hex, rgb(), or hsl() with literal numbers). A raw
 * CSS variable like "var(--primary)" cannot be parsed to HSL at render time; pass the
 * concrete brand color instead, or use the default palette and tint via CSS if you need
 * variable-driven theming.
 */
